## 摘要

混合专家（MoE）模型的专家卸载使单 GPU 运行大模型成为可能，但其延迟瓶颈在于每层 top-k 专家的 PCIe 传输。预测式预取被广泛寄予厚望，然而已有工作的结论相互矛盾：有的报告大幅收益，有的在真实负载上反而劣化。本文在统一实验床（DeepSeek-V2-Lite，27 层 64 专家 top-6）与统一真实路由 trace（UltraChat 250 prompts，8.29M 专家请求）上系统回答三个问题。**其一，预测准确率值多少？** 合成预测器元分析表明价值空间巨大（LRU 到完美预取的 miss 跨度达 21×）、盈亏平衡准确率低至 p*≈0.4，且预取可超越 Belady 按需最优。**其二，训练成本能买多少提前量？** 逐层 MLP 与训练自由 residual gate 的 ahead=1..12 衰减定律表明：MLP 看 12 层的准确率（0.6608）≈ residual 看 1 层（0.6664），半衰期 38.8 层对 18.1 层。**其三，收益为何难以兑现？** 我们构建带宽感知缓存-预取模拟器，发现无限带宽假设下的 miss 排序与带宽受限下的 TPOT 排序完全颠倒；有效预取窗口由 ⌈传输时间/层时⌉（≈2 层）而非预测剖面（可达 12 层）决定，统一 ahead=2 在全部 9 个（带宽×容量）组合下最优（+24.1% TPOT），逐层差异化调度为负结果；置信度准入在标定 PCIe 带宽下同样无效（最低置信槽位 precision 仍达 0.70），仅在通道饱和区（bw=1）出现交叉（fan-out=4 反超 top-6）。本文的核心信息可概括为：**预测、提前量、准入三个杠杆各自由不同瓶颈定价——预测由 miss 价值曲线定价（入场便宜），提前量由带宽定价（≈2 层封顶），准入由通道饱和度定价（分区有效）**；据此给出的设计点（逐层 MLP + 统一 ahead=2 + top-6 全准入 + LRU）在标定带宽下达模拟上界 +24.1% TPOT。

## Abstract

Expert offloading makes large Mixture-of-Experts models servable on a single GPU, but per-token latency is dominated by PCIe transfers of the top-k experts per layer. Predictive prefetching is widely believed to help, yet published results are contradictory. On a unified testbed (DeepSeek-V2-Lite, 27 layers × 64 experts, top-6) and a unified real routing trace (UltraChat, 8.29M expert requests), we answer three questions. (1) *How much is prediction accuracy worth?* An oracle meta-analysis shows a 21× miss-rate headroom from LRU to perfect prefetching, a break-even accuracy of only p*≈0.4, and that prefetching can beat Belady's demand-fetch optimum. (2) *How much lookahead does training buy?* Measuring the ahead=1..12 accuracy decay of learned per-layer MLP predictors against the training-free residual-gate predictor, we find MLP at 12 layers ahead (0.6608) matches residual-gate at 1 layer ahead (0.6664), with a 2.1× longer half-life (38.8 vs 18.1 layers). (3) *Why do gains fail to materialize?* A bandwidth-aware cache-prefetch simulator reveals that the miss-rate ranking under infinite bandwidth is *reversed* under bandwidth constraints; the effective prefetch window is set by ⌈transfer time / layer time⌉ (≈2 layers), not by the predictability profile (up to 12 layers); uniform ahead=2 is optimal across all 9 (bandwidth × capacity) combinations (+24.1% TPOT), while per-layer differentiated lookahead is a negative result. Confidence-based admission is likewise unprofitable at calibrated PCIe bandwidth (the lowest-confidence slots still carry 0.70 precision) and only pays off in the channel-saturated regime (bw=1), where fan-out=4 overtakes top-6. Our takeaway: the three levers—prediction, lookahead, admission—are priced by three different bottlenecks.

